{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>And Moshe gave, etc., as YHWH commanded, etc.</b> It is difficult: after the verse said <b>by the mouth of HaShem</b>, what place is there to say <b>as YHWH commanded</b>, etc.? And it appears that since this act contains a benefit for Aharon his brother and his sons, and there is room to say that Moshe had personal satisfaction in benefiting his brother — therefore the verse comes and removes the possibility of this intention from Moshe, that he did not think in this act of any desire to give to his brother, but rather to fulfill the word of HaShem was his purpose in his deed."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:57.390855583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}